 "prompt": "Text:\n{text}",
 "max_lines": 12,
 "instructions": "You label what Reddit authors say about themselves.\n\nRead the text and list the facts its author states about themselves that are true at the time of writing. A fact counts when the author says it outright or it follows necessarily from what they say about themselves; for example \"my husband\" means married, and a tag like \"28F\" means age 28 and female.\n\nLeave out:\n- anything about other people, including quoted lines that start with >\n- questions, hypotheticals, jokes, sarcasm, role-play, wishes and plans\n- past states that may no longer hold, such as a former job or a previous home\n- guesses from the topic, the writing style or the community the text was posted in\n- values worked out from another fact, such as a generation from an age, a birth year from an age, a country from a city, or an education from a job\n\nWrite one line \"field: value\" per fact, at most one value per field, in lowercase. Where a field lists values, use one of them exactly; if none fits, leave the field out. If the text states none of these facts, answer: none\n\nFields:\n{fields}",
